# /etc/indy-nexus/allowed_signers
#
# List of SSH public keys trusted to sign commits that the auto-updater
# will accept. Copy this file to /etc/indy-nexus/allowed_signers on the
# LXC (drop the .example suffix) and replace the placeholder line with
# your real public key(s).
#
# Format (one key per line, OpenSSH allowed_signers format):
#
#   <principal>   <key-type> <base64-pubkey> [comment]
#
# - <principal> is the email address recorded as the git committer/author.
#   It MUST match the email on the commits you expect to accept (run
#   `git log -1 --pretty=%ce` to see it). Wildcards like "*@example.com"
#   are allowed but not recommended for this use case.
# - <key-type> <base64-pubkey> is the literal contents of your public key
#   file (e.g. ~/.ssh/indy_signing_ed25519.pub), minus the trailing
#   comment.
#
# Example (replace with your own values):
#
# markwulk@gmail.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3Nza...REPLACE_ME...4nS9F indy.nexus signing key
#
# After editing, lock the file down:
#
#   sudo chown root:root /etc/indy-nexus/allowed_signers
#   sudo chmod 0644       /etc/indy-nexus/allowed_signers
#
# To add a second trusted signer later (e.g. a teammate or a second
# machine of your own), just append another line.
